<title>Kawasaki Disease: Management.</title>
<graphic href="eee0849-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Fever for &#x2265;5 days; assess patient for features of Kawasaki disease (<xref ref="table001" />).</label>
<path target="cell-2">Fewer than 2 criteria</path>
<path target="cell-3">2 or 3 criteria present</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-2">
<label>Consider other diagnosis.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Principal laboratory results (<xref ref="table002" />) consistent with systemic inflammation.</label>
<path target="cell-4">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-5">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-4">
<label>3 or more supplemental laboratory criteria (<xref ref="table002" />) present.</label>
<path target="cell-6">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-7">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Treat patient and order echocardiogram.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-7">
<label>Echocardiogram.</label>
<path target="cell-8">Positive</path>
<path target="cell-9">Negative</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Treat patient.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-9">
<label>Repeat echocardiogram if fever persists; if fever resolves, consider other diagnosis.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-5">
<label>Daily followup.</label>
<path target="cell-13">Fever persists</path>
<path target="cell-10">Fever resolves</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-10">
<label>Assess for peeling typical of KD.</label>
<path target="cell-11">Present</path>
<path target="cell-12">Absent</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-11">
<label>Echocardiogram.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-12">
<label>No further followup needed.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-13">
<label>Reassess for features of Kawasaki disease (above).</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>Data from American Heart Association. Diagnosis, treatment, and long-term management of Kawasaki disease: a statement for health professionals from the Committee on Rheumatic Fever, Endocarditis and Kawasaki Disease, Council on Cardiovascular Disease in the Young. 2004. [http:&#x002F;&#x002F;www.guidelines.gov&#x002F;summary&#x002F;summary.aspx?view&#x005F;id&#x003D;1&amp;doc&#x005F;id&#x003D;6180].</footnote>
</footnotes>
